  "body": "### What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nPorts the existing MoE router-replay (RL) wiring from Qwen3.5-MoE to Qwen4-Exp. The patched `Qwen4ExpTextSparseMoeBlock.forward` now keeps `router_logits` from the router and, when a replay manager is installed via `veomni.utils.moe_router_replay.set_active_replay`, substitutes `selected_experts` with previously recorded target indices and recomputes the post-topk routing weights — exactly the same contract as the Qwen3.5-MoE integration:\r\n```\r\nif get_active_replay() is not None:\r\n    routing_scores = softmax(router_logits, float32)\r\n    selected_experts = maybe_replay_indices(self.gate, routing_scores, selected_experts)\r\n    routing_weights = gather(routing_scores, selected_experts) / sum(..., keepdim=True)\r\n\r\n```\r\nWhen no manager is installed, the only added cost is a single `is not None` check and behavior is byte-identical to native routing.\r\n\r\nNo changes to `veomni/utils/moe_router_replay.py` are needed — its wired-family registry already lists `qwen4_exp`; this PR makes the generated modeling code actually fire the hook.\r\n### Checklist Before Starting\r\n\r\n- Search for relative PRs/issues and link here: None\r\n- PR title follows `[{modules}] {type}: {description}` format (enforced by [check_pr_title.yml](workflows/check_pr_title.yml))\r\n  - **Allowed modules:** `agent`, `ci`, `ckpt`, `config`, `data`, `dist`, `docker`, `docs`, `logging`, `lora`, `misc`, `model`, `omni`, `optim`, `ops`, `parallel`, `perf`, `release`, `task`, `trainer`\r\n  - **Allowed types:** `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `test`\r\n  - Breaking changes: prepend `[BREAKING]` — e.g. `[BREAKING][parallel, model] feat: dynamic batching`\r\n\r\n### Test\r\n\r\nNo new CI test added (per the three-option rule, with reason):\r\n\r\n- This is a mechanical, structurally identical port: `Qwen4ExpTextSparseMoeBlock.forward` is byte-for-byte isomorphic to `Qwen3_5MoeSparseMoeBlock.forward` (gate returns `(router_logits, post-softmax scores, indices)`; shared-expert blend; out-of-place add), so the replay insertion point and the post-topk math (softmax recompute → `maybe_replay_indices` → gather → renorm → dtype cast) are identical to the already-tested Qwen3.5-MoE path.\r\n- Core manager semantics (record/replay, passthrough when inactive) are already covered by the CI-enumerated `tests/utils/test_moe_router_replay.py`.\r\n- `tests/models/test_moe_router_replay_invariants.py` currently wires `qwen3_moe` / `qwen3_5_moe`; wiring `qwen4_exp` into the same invariants harness is a clean follow-up (happy to do it in this PR if preferred).\r\n- Local validation performed: patchgen-consistency check of the config sources, `py_compile` of both generated modeling files and the config, and an import smoke test under the pinned `veomni` env (`transformers==5.16.1`, NPU path `patched_modeling_qwen4_exp_npu.py` imports and exposes `Qwen4ExpTextSparseMoeBlock`).\r\n\r\n### API and Usage Example\r\n\r\nNo public API change (model-side wiring only). RL framework usage is unchanged from the other MoE families:\r\n\r\n### Design & Code Changes\r\n\r\n1. `veomni/models/transformers/qwen4_exp/qwen4_exp_gpu_patch_gen_config.py` (+51): \r\n   - `config.add_import(\"veomni.utils.moe_router_replay\", names=[\"get_active_replay\", \"maybe_replay_indices\"])`;\r\n   - new `@config.override_method(\"Qwen4ExpTextSparseMoeBlock.forward\", …)`: switch gate unpack to keep `router_logits`, insert the replay block before `self.experts(...)`, keep the shared-expert out-of-place add.\r\n2. `veomni/models/transformers/qwen4_exp/qwen4_exp_npu_patch_gen_config.py`: no change — it `deepcopys` the GPU config, so the NPU path inherits automatically.\r\n3. Generated: `generated/patched_modeling_qwen4_exp_gpu.py` and `_npu.py` — minimal, byte-identical patch (+22/−1 each: one import + one forward hunk). A full `patchgen` regen was deliberately not committed because the current patchgen version re-normalizes the import block (≈119-line churn, unrelated to this change); the checked-in files are kept as a minimal diff that is semantically equivalent to the regen output. Regen on the pinned toolchain (`veomni` env, `transformers==5.16.1`) reproduces the same replay code.\r\n4. `veomni/utils/moe_router_replay.py`: untouched (`qwen4_exp` is already in its wired families).\r\n\r\n### Checklist Before Submitting\r\n\r\n- Read the [Contribute Guide](https://github.com/ByteDance-Seed/VeOmni/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- Applied pre-commit checks\r\n- Added/updated documentation\r\n- If `tasks/` training scripts were moved or renamed: updated `docs/` examples and verified `python3 scripts/ci/check_doc_task_paths.py` passes (also enforced by the **Check doc task paths** CI workflow)\r\n- Tests: extended an existing CI-enumerated test, **or** added a new test and wired it into `gpu_unit_tests.yml` (and `npu_unit_tests.yml` where applicable), **or** explained in **Test** why none is needed. Note that CI enumerates test files individually — a new file outside `tests/data/` and `tests/ops/` does not run until it is listed. See [.agents/knowledge/testing.md](../.agents/knowledge/testing.md).\r\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added router replay support for Qwen4-Exp, allowing replayed expert selections to be used with routing weights recalculated for those selections. When replay is inactive, the model continues to use its original expert selections and weights. The feature supports both normalized and unnormalized top-k routing and preserves the shared-expert contribution to the model output.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
